 * load/store pairs, MIPS32r2 bit-field instructions and the subset of the
 * FPU that the compiler emits) and implements the Linux system calls the
 * program makes (open/read/write/close/lseek/... , time, exit, ...) by
 * forwarding them to the host operating system / node.js filesystem.
 *
 * Usage:
 *     node vm.js [options] [elf-file]
 *
 * Options:
 *   --max-seconds=N   stop after N seconds of emulation
 *   --max-frames=N    stop after N rendered frames have been saved
 *   --frames-dir=DIR  where copies of every rendered frame are stored
 *   --trace           print a trace of the last instructions on a fault
